CompilerError:
error E2015: <fragment>:4:10: Unsupported: a function with 65 argument slots — more than the 64 a call can carry. A signature's slots are its declared parameters plus the hidden ones the ABI adds (a companion environment per function-typed parameter, a layout descriptor for a generic that reads `sizeof`, one witness per `where` constraint), and the limit is the width of the per-argument float mask that routes each one to its register file
